From 2bce9d12521f51834f536b25b659317477eaf3b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: George Moussalem <george.moussalem@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 07:29:47 +0400
Subject: [PATCH ath-next 14/15] wifi: ath11k: add multipd support for QCN6122
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
Message-Id: <20260916-ipq5018-qcn6122-mpd-v1-14-a4e47531e63f@outlook.com>

IPQ5018/QCN6122 boards follow the multi PD (protection domains)
architecture where the root PD manages the life cycle of the user PDs
(radio instances). This topology avoids having one instance of the
running Q6 firmware crashing resulting in crashing the others.

The IPQ5018 platform can come with one or two optional QCN6122 wifi
cards. To differentiate the two, the user PD instance number (1 or 2) is
added to the QMI service instance ID so the QCN6122 firmware knows which
radio instance to use and on what PCIe rail it is on.

On IPQ5018/QCN6122 boards, the default mapping is as follows:

          +-> User PD 1 ----> IPQ5018 Internal 2.4G Radio
         /
        /
Root PD +---> User PD 2 ----> QCN6122 5G/6G Radio on PCIE1
        \
         \
          +-> User PD 3 ----> QCN6102 5G/6G Radio on PCIE0

Signed-off-by: George Moussalem <george.moussalem@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c | 8 ++++++++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.h | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
@@ -937,6 +937,14 @@ static int ath11k_ahb_init_userpd(struct
 
 		ab_ahb->userpd_id = userpd_id;
 		break;
+	case ATH11K_HW_QCN6122_HW10:
+		if (userpd_id != ATH11K_AHB_USERPD_ID_2 &&
+		    userpd_id != ATH11K_AHB_USERPD_ID_3)
+			return -EINVAL;
+
+		ab_ahb->userpd_id = userpd_id;
+		ab->qmi.service_ins_id += (ab_ahb->userpd_id - 1);
+		break;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.h
@@ -28,6 +28,8 @@
 
 enum ath11k_ahb_userpd_id {
 	ATH11K_AHB_USERPD_ID_1 = 1,
+	ATH11K_AHB_USERPD_ID_2,
+	ATH11K_AHB_USERPD_ID_3,
 	ATH11K_AHB_USERPD_ID_MAX,
 };
 
